/*!
    \title Custom Linear Scale
    \ingroup quickgraphlibdemos
    \brief Demonstrates custom tick formatting with binned image data.
    \example customlinearscale

    \image examples/CustomLinearScale.png

    This example demonstrates how to display a 256×256 binned image with custom tick labels that represent 
    the underlying data scale. The image bins are mapped to a 0-100M range, with tick labels formatted to 
    display in millions with an "M" suffix (e.g., "20M" instead of "20000000"), making the graph much more readable.

    The example shows:
    - Displaying binned image data (256×256) using \l{ColorMesh}
    - Setting viewRect to match bin dimensions for direct coordinate mapping
    - Converting bin coordinates to actual values in tick labels
    - Creating custom tick delegates with formatted text
    - Applying the custom formatting to both axes consistently

    This approach is useful when working with large numerical ranges in binned or pixelated data, such as 
    sensor readings, histograms, or scientific imaging data.

    \quotefile examples/CustomLinearScale.qml
*/

